==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|þwahan|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|þwahan|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|dwahan|lang=goh}}, Old Norse {{term|þvá}}, Gothic {{term|𐌸𐍅𐌰𐌷𐌰𐌽|tr=þwahan|sc=Goth}}. The Germanic base is also the source of English {{term|towel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/θwæ:an/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
'''þwēan''' (class VI strong: '''þweahþ''' ‘he washes’; '''þwōh''' ‘he washed’; '''þwōgon''' ‘they washed’; past participle '''ġeþwagen''')

# to [[wash]], [[anoint]]

